File Index

/AreaHeaderEditor.tsx
Purpose: #AREA header form (name/credits/vnum range) with an inline warning when the range no longer covers a defined vnum; the server enforces the same shrink guard plus overlap-vs-area.lst on save.

/AreasPage.test.tsx
Purpose: Phase 11 tests: conditional save sends/refreshes baseHash, 409 → conflict panel (save-anyway resends WITHOUT hash; reload refetches and clears), presence badge + banner rendering from mocked /api/presence. 2026-07-26: openTiny() now waits for the "Save" button instead of the removed "UI editor" tab label (the form/manual tab toggle is gone — the dashboard is always visible, Manual edit is just a toggle button now, same as every other tab).

/AreasPage.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26 Areas dashboard redesign) Areas tab — migrated OFF its hand-rolled duplicate state onto the shared useAreaWorkbench() (retiring the debt called out in this plan's research: it used to reimplement openArea/doSave/doReload/conflict handling/etc. identically to workbench.tsx). Left nav (AreaSidebar, now with onBeforeOpen=wb.confirmDiscard('switch areas') + an extraToolbar slot for the Import toggle — both new AreaSidebar props, see workbench.tsx) + AreaHeaderEditor stay as before. The room-list-nav + single-room-detail split is GONE, replaced by a room-name/vnum filter input above a scrollable list of RoomDashboardEntry (one per room, fully editable — not read-only) with a focusRoomVnum state auto-expanding whichever room a just-added room, a World-dashboard initialTarget, or a resolved preview-ref click points at. "+ Add room" lives here again (was Rooms-tab-only from 2026-07-26 morning to afternoon — now both tabs can add/delete, matching "Areas allows functionally what each focused view allows"). onEditRoom prop REMOVED (Areas doesn't need to hand off editing to Rooms anymore — it edits directly); onGoToResets/onGoToMap/onGoToMobs/onGoToScripts added, threaded straight through to each RoomDashboardEntry's blocked-delete panel (same shape as RoomsPage.tsx's own). 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): its own addNewRoom now fires a success toast too (matches RoomsPage.tsx's).

/DeleteBlockersPanel.test.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26) categorizeBlocker prefix-sniffing over each known deleteBlockers() shape (reset/exit/shop/special/script/unknown); panel groups blockers by category and only renders a "Go fix it" button for a category when its callback prop was actually supplied.

/DeleteBlockersPanel.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26) Categorized, actionable "why can't I delete this" panel — replaces a flat error toast on a blocked delete. categorizeBlocker(where) sniffs deleteBlockers()'s where-string prefix (services/merc-area/src/validate.ts collectRefs' fixed vocabulary: "reset #" / " exit " / "shop:"|"special:" / "script") into resets/map/mobs/scripts/other; renders one group per category present with its items, plus a "Go fix it →" button only for categories whose navigation callback (onGoToResets/onGoToMap/onGoToMobs/onGoToScripts) was supplied by the caller. Also exports useDeleteWithBlockers(wb, kind) — the check-blockers/confirm/remove flow itself (deleteBlockers + window.confirm + model-ops' removeEntity), co-located so it can't drift from the panel it feeds; RoomsPage.tsx's deleteRoom was refactored onto it (its own tests passed unmodified) and it's the intended path for the dashboard's per-room delete (Step 5); now also adopted by MobsPage.tsx/ObjectsPage.tsx (2026-07-26 UX polish pass) — Socials was investigated and explicitly excluded (no RefKind for socials, structurally nothing can reference one, deleteBlockers would never find anything). useDeleteWithBlockers's attemptDelete now also fires a success toast on removal (`wb.ok(\`removed ${kind} #${vnum}\`)`) — centralizing this here means every one of its 3 consumers (Rooms/Mobs/Objects) gets it for free, consistently worded.

/ImportAreaPanel.test.tsx
Purpose: Import panel tests: clean validate→commit (overwrite defaults false), error-blocked commit, explicit-overwrite gating for existing files, writes-off disable, stale-report invalidation on input change, resolved external-ref listing.

/ImportAreaPanel.tsx
Purpose: .are import panel (Phase 10) — file picker/paste → server quarantine report (blocking errors, warnings, resolved external refs, entity summary, canonical text with download) → commit gated on clean report + explicit overwrite checkbox; any input change invalidates the report.

/MobPlacementAccordion.test.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26) Renders mob prototype fields + this placement's reset row + Equipment/Scripts counts; editing MobEditor updates the shared prototype; +Give/+Equip insert contiguously after the block (asserted via the resets array's total length, not just the visible count); Remove this placement drops the M row AND its rider together (no orphan left behind); an undefined mob vnum (cross-area) shows a warning instead of crashing/rendering MobEditor.

/MobPlacementAccordion.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26) One `M` reset nested under RoomDashboardEntry — embeds MobEditor (edits the SHARED mob prototype, same vnum as the Mobs tab, explicitly labeled as such), the M row's own fields via ResetRowFields, a nested "Equipment" accordion (this placement's contiguous `G`/`E` riders — inserting via addRider splices immediately after the block since computeBlocks only groups CONTIGUOUS riders), and a nested "Scripts" accordion (area-wide MobScript rows filtered by mobVnum, via scripts-model.ts's useAreaScripts — deliberately different scoping semantics from Equipment, kept visually separate). "Remove this placement" drops the M row and all its riders in one setResets call. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): "Remove this placement" now requires a window.confirm naming the mob vnum + rider count (individual Equipment-row ✕ buttons stay unconfirmed on purpose — fine-grained, high-frequency, trivially undoable) and fires a success toast on removal.

/ObjectPlacementAccordion.test.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26) Renders object prototype fields + this placement's reset row + Contents; +Add item inside inserts a new P row contiguous with the existing run (contentsOf, reset-editing.tsx); Remove this placement drops the O row and its P contents together.

/ObjectPlacementAccordion.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26) One `O` reset nested under RoomDashboardEntry — embeds ObjectEditor (edits the SHARED object prototype, same vnum as the Objects tab), the O row's own fields, and a "Contents" accordion built from contentsOf (reset-editing.tsx) — the contiguous run of `P` rows whose arg3 matches THIS placement's object vnum ("P fills the closest O above it", ResetsPage's own help text — NOT grouped by computeBlocks, which only groups M+G/E/P). No scripts sub-accordion — script attachment is mob/room only, objects have none. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): "Remove this placement" now requires a window.confirm naming the object vnum + content-item count (individual Contents-row ✕ buttons stay unconfirmed, same reasoning as Equipment rows) and fires a success toast on removal.

