/RoomConnections.tsx
Purpose: Read-only "how does this room fit into the area" panel (2026-07-26) — for each of room.exits, direction (DOOR_NAMES), resolved target room name if it's in the same area's own rooms section (else an "external / not in this area" note), and lock state (LOCK_STATES). Pure presentation, no fetches, no mutation. Shared by RoomsPage.tsx and RoomDashboardEntry.tsx (Areas dashboard redesign) — one exit-rendering implementation, multiple call sites.

/RoomDashboardEntry.test.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26) Closed by default (summary counts only, no form fields in the DOM's visible sense); opening reveals RoomEditor + RoomConnections + Mobs/Objects/Progs groups with correct counts; RoomEditor edits round-trip; a blocked delete shows DeleteBlockersPanel with a working onGoToMap wiring + Dismiss clears it without deleting; +Place a mob/object here add new reset rows; the embedded RoomEditor's onOpenSpawn link still fires.

/RoomDashboardEntry.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26) One room in the Areas dashboard — a top-level `<details>` (closed by default, children conditionally rendered only while open, unlike the accordions nested inside it which rely on jsdom-visible-but-CSS-hidden native `<details>` semantics). Embeds RoomEditor directly (full edit, not read-only) + RoomConnections + a "Mobs in this room" fieldset (one MobPlacementAccordion per M-block whose room arg matches, via useResetsEditor) + an "Objects in this room" fieldset (one ObjectPlacementAccordion per matching O row) + RoomScriptsAccordion. Delete uses the shared useDeleteWithBlockers hook (DeleteBlockersPanel.tsx) — same categorized panel + "Go fix it" wiring as RoomsPage.tsx's own delete, via the same onGoToResets/onGoToMap/onGoToMobs/onGoToScripts prop shape. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): addMobPlacement/addObjectPlacement now fire a success toast naming the placed vnum + room.

/RoomEditor.test.tsx
Purpose: RoomEditor form round-trip and flag-toggle tests (incl. Phase 13's conditional "see what spawns here" link), the Phase 14b 10-door fix (7th+ exit addable, all 10 compass names offered, cap now sits at 10), the room extra-descriptions add/edit/remove round trip and an exit's independent look-text edit + AreasPage gating/header-editor/new-area tests. Also fixed a real pre-existing race in the new-area-creation test (clicking "+ New area" before /api/capabilities resolved could hit it while still disabled) — surfaced, not caused, by that session's other test additions in the same file. 2026-07-26 (Areas dashboard redesign, Step 6): rewritten to match Areas being editable again — "rooms are directly editable (expand the accordion, no read-only view)" (click the room's `<summary>` text; jsdom fires a native `<details>` toggle on click, confirmed empirically — no manual DOM/event hackery needed), the old "Edit this room fires onEditRoom" test removed (that callback no longer exists — Areas doesn't hand off editing anymore) and replaced with a plain onOpenSpawn-only test, and "no room-mutation UI is offered" INVERTED to "room-mutation UI IS offered" (+ Add room / Delete room buttons now exist).

/RoomEditor.tsx
Purpose: Form-first room editor (mb-field idiom the other editors follow): name/description, sector/heal/mana, room flags, an extra-descriptions fieldset (2026-07-26, mirrors ObjectEditor.tsx's add/edit/remove keyword+text pattern exactly — the data layer already round-tripped Room.extraDescrs, this closed the last UI-only gap), exits table (Phase 14b: addExit/the +add-exit cap now span all 10 DOOR_NAMES doors, not the pre-12b 6-door leftover; 2026-07-26: each exit row also gained an optional look-text textarea for RoomExit.description, on its own line below the dense row so the row itself stays scannable); optional onOpenSpawn (Phase 13) renders a link that hands the room vnum up to App.tsx's resetsRoomTarget lift, landing on the Resets tab's Simulate pane filtered to this room. Used by features/rooms/RoomsPage.tsx (cross-directory) AND embedded directly inside features/areas/RoomDashboardEntry.tsx (Areas dashboard redesign) — both are real editors, not a read-only/editor split. Phase G: header gained a SaveAsSnippetButton (features/content) — same shared component every entity editor embeds, so both the standalone Rooms tab AND every Areas-dashboard room accordion get it for free with no prop-signature change.

/RoomScriptsAccordion.test.tsx
