/RoomScriptsAccordion.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26) "Progs" in the user's own words — this room's MobScript rows (attach:'room', mobVnum holding the ROOM's own vnum) via scripts-model.ts's useAreaScripts, each embedding ScriptEditor in a per-script nested `<details>`. Area-wide data scoped to one room identity (unlike MobPlacementAccordion's per-placement equipment) — no block/index juggling needed. Shared by RoomDashboardEntry.tsx.

/areas.css
Purpose: All builder styling — sidebar/toolbar/toast, compact form system (mb-field label-above inputs, mb-fieldset groups, mb-form-grid, mb-dice-row, mb-flag-grid, mb-form width cap), preview/diff colors, world dashboard table, Phase 10 import panel + audit table, Phase 11 presence badge/banner, conflict panel, ref-link buttons (incl. Phase 13's mb-room-spawn-link and 2026-07-26's mb-room-edit-link), Phase 13 Simulate pane (mb-spawn-room accordion, mb-spawn-list/gear/contents nesting, mb-spawn-warnings), 2026-07-26: mb-connections-list (RoomConnections' exit list), mb-delete-blockers/-group (DeleteBlockersPanel, same palette as mb-conflict), and mb-dashboard-room/-room-body/-accordion/-accordion--nested/-subitems (the Areas dashboard redesign's nested room/mob/object/prog accordions). mb-room-readonly-actions/-descr REMOVED (Step 6) — Areas' read-only room view no longer exists, replaced by the dashboard. UX polish pass: mb-toast--warn/--info added alongside the existing --ok/--err (same palette family — dark background, light text); mb-unsaved-indicator (WorkbenchToolbar's "● unsaved changes").

/model-ops.test.ts
Purpose: Vnum allocation, template emit/parse round trip, and delete-blocking tests.

/model-ops.ts
Purpose: Pure create/delete model operations — nextFreeVnum (single-namespace range allocation), bootable mob/object/room templates, section-aware insertion, removeEntity, deleteBlockers (reverse refs computed on the post-delete model), shop/special ops (getShop/upsertShop/removeShop, getSpecial/setSpecial/removeSpecial), social ops (socialsOf/newSocialTemplate/upsertSocial/removeSocial; blank fields map to `$`).

/scripts-model.ts
Purpose: (2026-07-26) useAreaScripts(wb) — the #SCRIPTS array + set/add/update/remove closures over a shared AreaWorkbench, same "get section, set section" shape as reset-editing.tsx's useResetsEditor. Returns {script, index} pairs (original index preserved) so callers can filter the SAME array (by attach/mobVnum) without losing the index needed to mutate the right row. Shared by MobPlacementAccordion.tsx's Scripts sub-accordion and RoomScriptsAccordion.tsx — both filter this one array, area-wide, never a per-room copy. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass): addScript/removeScript now also fire a success toast (wb.ok) — centralized here so both consumers get consistent wording for free; updateScript deliberately does NOT toast (every field keystroke would spam it).

/workbench.test.tsx
Purpose: (2026-07-26) Dirty-state tests via renderHook: clean after openArea, dirty after any setAreaModel, clean again after doSave or a re-openArea (reload); confirmDiscard short-circuits true when clean and only calls window.confirm when dirty. UX polish pass (Step 5): beforeunload is registered only once dirty (spies on window.addEventListener), the handler actually calls preventDefault on a real Event, and it's deregistered again after a successful save.

/workbench.tsx
Purpose: useAreaWorkbench shared state/actions (open area w/ baseHash, preview, download, gated conditional save with 409 conflict handling + reload/save-anyway, reload, manual raw-text edit with parse-validated back-apply, createArea) + Phase 11 usePresence (20s heartbeat+poll, silent failures)/othersEditing + shared widgets: AreaSidebar (presence badges), NewAreaForm, WorkbenchToolbar (presence banner + conflict panel), ConflictPanel, PresenceBanner, PresenceBadge, WorkbenchManualPane, WorkbenchToast, FlagGrid, WordInput, NumField, TextField. 2026-07-26: gained isDirty (a synced-snapshot-vs-current-area JSON compare, snapshot reset on openArea/doSave/conflictSaveAnyway) + confirmDiscard(actionLabel) (true when clean, window.confirm's when dirty) — the dirty-state baseline AreasPage.tsx (Step 6) wires into its area-switcher; snapshot is state (not a ref) specifically so setting it re-triggers the isDirty useMemo. AreaSidebar also gained two OPTIONAL props: onBeforeOpen(file)=>boolean (a guard run before switching areas) and extraToolbar (ReactNode rendered between "+ New area" and the area list; AreasPage uses it for its "Import .are file…" toggle) — lets AreasPage stop hand-rolling its own sidebar markup. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass, Step 5): onBeforeOpen={() => wb.confirmDiscard('switch areas')} is now wired in EVERY tab that renders AreaSidebar (Areas/Rooms/Mobs/Objects/Resets/Socials — Scripts/Map don't use this shared component, see their own .annotated entries for their equivalent guards). The hook also gained a beforeunload effect (registers only while isDirty, cleaned up on save/reload/unmount) — covers every consumer automatically, no per-page wiring needed. WorkbenchToolbar renders a small "● unsaved changes" indicator (mb-unsaved-indicator, areas.css) next to the filename whenever wb.isDirty. 2026-07-26 (UX polish pass, Step 1): the local `Toast` type/`WorkbenchToast` rendering were extracted to features/shared/Toast.tsx (ToastState/Toast component) — WorkbenchToast is now a thin wrapper over it, zero behavior change for existing callers. The hook's private `ok`/`err` closures were joined by `warn`/`info` and ALL FOUR promoted onto the returned AreaWorkbench object (previously only `err`/`setToast` were exposed — pages had no way to toast a success without reaching into `setToast` directly). `Toast` (this file's local type alias) is now just `ToastState` re-exported for back-compat.
